    "updated_at": "2026-11-20T05:43:08Z",
    "body": "fix on issue/2394-cone-thread · PR #2883 · pinned by example_catalog::turning_cone_thread_case_posts_the_taper_and_the_thread, every_catalog_case_opens_regenerates_verifies_and_posts_byte_for_byte, every_catalog_case_rebuilds_from_camscript · merges at the next cut\n\nBugs found on the way, each filed as its own issue:\n\n- #2878 (`P1`): a G76 cycle starts inside the part. The control moves the insert into the material at rapid.\n- #2879 (`P3`): a threading pass cannot start in front of the end face.\n- #2880 (`P3`): Profile Finish reads thread valleys and a neck step as rest.\n- #2881 (`P3`): a steep fillet chord sends the profile ride far out of the bar.\n- #2882 (`P3`): the profile rides post runs of identical `G01` blocks.\n\nBecause of them the case differs from the issue text in three points:\n\n- It imports two models (the turned blank and the finished part).\n- It posts the thread as G32 passes, not as the G76 cycle.\n- It has a sixth operation, a Groove Finish for the neck.\n\n`docs/decisions/2394-cone-thread.md` gives the reasons. No catalog threading insert fits a 1.5 mm pitch (#893), so the script defines one.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
